{"name":"Summer’s Eve","hex":"#a97069","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"summer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of four seasons, traditionally the second, marked by the longest and typically hottest days of the year due to the inclination of the Earth and thermal lag. Typically regarded as spanning  either the period between the summer solstice to the autumnal equinox, or the months of June, July, and August in the Northern Hemisphere and the months of December, January and February in the Southern Hemisphere.","year; used to give the age of a person, usually a young one."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the summer, as in a particular place on holiday."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summer"},{"term":"eve","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Even."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The day or night before, usually used for holidays, such as Christmas Eve.","Evening, night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eve"}],"entries":[{"title":"Summer's Eve","blocks":[{"text":"Summer's Eve is an American brand of feminine hygiene products that is produced by the C.B. Fleet Company, a subsidiary of Prestige Consumer Healthcare."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer's_Eve","wikidata":"Q7637226"},{"title":"Eve","blocks":[{"text":"Eve is a figure from the Book of Genesis in the Old Testament. According to the origin story of the Abrahamic religions, she was the first woman to be created by God. Eve is known also as Adam's wife."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eve","wikidata":"Q830183"},{"title":"Summer","blocks":[{"text":"Summer or summertime is the hottest and brightest of the four temperate seasons, occurring after spring and before autumn. Starting on the summer solstice, daylight hours are the longest and darkness hours are the shortest, with day length decreasing as the season progresses after the solstice. In the Northern Hemisphere, summer is usually defined as starting on June 21 or 22, and ending on September 22 or 23; and in the Southern Hemisphere, as the period between December 22 or 23 and March 20 or 21."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg/330px-Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer","wikidata":"Q1313"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Eva.jpg/500px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Eva.jpg/500px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Eva.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Orvieto060.jpg/500px-Orvieto060.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Orvieto060.jpg/1280px-Orvieto060.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Orvieto060.jpg/500px-Orvieto060.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Creation of Eve, marble relief by Lorenzo Maitani on the Orvieto Cathedral, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrvieto060.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Heyerdahl_adam_og_eva.jpg/500px-Heyerdahl_adam_og_eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Heyerdahl_adam_og_eva.jpg/500px-Heyerdahl_adam_og_eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam